# `eol=lf` pins the worktree, not just the index. `docker COPY` takes worktree bytes, so CRLF in a
# checkout breaks `tests/docker/`'s images: shell scripts fail with `$'\r': command not found`, unit
# `ExecStart` lines carry a trailing `\r`, and `.version` reads back as `dietpi\r`. Applied to
# everything so a file added to an image is covered without a per-extension rule.
#
# This does not cover files written by Python: `pathlib.Path.write_text` translates `\n` to `\r\n`
# on Windows, so use `write_bytes` or a `sed -i` in the image for those.
* text=auto eol=lf
